HDMI audio in the control app
-----------------------------
Beta2 enables stereo 48 kHz S16_LE LPCM HDMI capture alongside video by default.
An explicit audio_experimental=0 option still disables it.
Stereo-tone and short concurrent OBS tests passed, and the maintainer confirmed
music capture end to end. The audio toggle uses a narrow polkit helper to reload
an idle driver with supported options preserved; HDMI briefly reconnects.
Other capture clients must close first. The toggle changes no boot configuration.
Video stop or HDMI recovery can interrupt audio with an XRUN; restart audio if
needed. Long-duration stability and A/V synchronization remain unqualified.
The kernel option is still named audio_experimental for compatibility with
existing configurations; its name does not indicate the current feature label.

Issue reports
-------------
Save a report from the control app while the failure is present, review it,
then choose Report a problem on GitHub. Include source mode, capture settings
and reproduction steps. Reports add distro, kernel, package/module details and
audio DMA counters without recording media or uploading automatically.
CLI: /usr/libexec/openlivegamer4k/collect-audio-report ./report.json
An existing output file is never overwritten. See the reporting guide at
https://github.com/royakem/OpenLiveGamer4K/blob/main/docs/REPORTING.md
